cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Quantiom: A browser-native, research-grade quantum circuit editor, simulator, and visualizer"
message: "If you use Quantiom in your research, please cite it using this metadata."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Andre
    family-names: Paquette
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0001-3961-9500"
repository-code: "https://github.com/thepacket/quantiom"
url: "https://quantiom.fly.dev"
abstract: >-
  Quantiom is a browser-native quantum circuit editor, simulator, and
  visualizer for users already comfortable with quantum-computing concepts.
  It runs entirely in the browser with no installation: a multi-tab 64-gate
  editor feeds a dense statevector simulator, an Aaronson-Gottesman stabilizer
  tableau, and a quantum-trajectory noise simulator, alongside ~40 research-
  grade panels including 24 entanglement and dynamics visualizers, OpenQASM 3
  round-trip, eight code/format exporters, optimizers, error mitigation, and a
  transpile/route/compile pipeline.
keywords:
  - quantum computing
  - quantum circuits
  - quantum simulation
  - scientific visualization
  - OpenQASM
  - TypeScript
license: MIT
version: 0.9.0
date-released: "2026-06-04"
